    ]
   },
   "section": "hook",
   "overlays": {
    "hook": "They called it Black Wall Street. *In less than a day, it was gone.*"
   },
   "captions": false,
   "speed": 1.4
  },
  {
   "id": "name",
   "text": "This is Greenwood, in Tulsa, Oklahoma.",
   "visual": {
    "kind": "title",
    "title": "Greenwood",
    "sub": "Tulsa, Oklahoma"
   },
   "section": "who"
  },
  {
   "id": "built",
   "text": "Tulsa was segregated. So Black Tulsans built their own district, north of the railroad tracks.",
   "visual": {
    "kind": "title",
    "title": "Built by Black Tulsans",
    "sub": "north of the Frisco tracks"
   },
   "section": "story",
   "overlays": {
    "stamp": "1900s"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "grow",
   "text": "By 1921, about ten thousand people lived there. Newspapers, churches, doctors, lawyers, and a movie theater, the Dreamland.",
   "visual": {
    "kind": "title",
    "title": "10,000 people",
    "sub": "Greenwood, 1921"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "spark",
   "text": "On May 31, 1921, a Black teenager was arrested, and a white mob gathered at the courthouse.",
   "visual": {
    "kind": "title",
    "title": "May 31, 1921",
    "sub": "Tulsa courthouse"
   },
   "section": "twist"
  },
  {
   "id": "dawn",
   "text": "At dawn, armed white men crossed the tracks. They looted homes, and set them on fire.",
   "visual": {
    "kind": "card",
    "image": "fire",
    "caption": "Greenwood on fire, June 1, 1921"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "ash",
   "text": "Thirty-five city blocks burned. About ten thousand people lost their homes.",
   "visual": {
    "kind": "card",
    "image": "district",
    "caption": "Part of the burned district, June 1921"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "toll",
   "text": "Historians believe up to three hundred people were killed. No one was ever sent to prison for it.",
   "visual": {
    "kind": "card",
    "image": "ruins",
    "caption": "Ruins in Greenwood, June 1921"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "tents",
   "text": "And for decades, the story was left out of the history books.",
   "visual": {
    "kind": "card",
    "image": "tents",
    "caption": "Red Cross tents, Tulsa, 1921"
   },
   "section": "legacy"
  },
  {
   "id": "rebuild",
   "text": "But Greenwood rebuilt, house by house.",
   "visual": {
    "kind": "card",
    "image": "rebuild",
    "caption": "Rebuilding Greenwood, 1921"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "end",
   "text": "They built it, and then they built it again.",
   "visual": {
    "kind": "photo",
    "image": "rebuild",
